WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.900
We are now going to bring in

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.003
Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.838
You have been watching this

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.339
since the beginning.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.741
You have been talking about this

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.075
since the beginning.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:09.976
The invasion happened,

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.045
I think on the 24th.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.414
I ended up on Poland on the 26th, as

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.882
thousands of refugees

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.151
were coming over the border from

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.120
from Ukraine.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.254
I'm curious

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.723
what your thoughts are on hearing

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.658
the President of the United States

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.426
in a country

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.660
that is currently in war

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.063
with sirens going off there are no U.S.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:30.530
troops there.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.465
And yet he says

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.200
we are going to stick with you

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.201
for the long haul.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:35.969
In other words,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.237
you have our full support.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.705
What does that mean to Ukraine?

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.607
What does that say to Russia

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.242
and the rest of the world?

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.343
Well, Sarah, good morning.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.712
This is a really big deal.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.647
And the way that the president

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.715
has orchestrated this

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.283
this would kind of be like

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.017
if Roosevelt

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.353
had visited London during the blitz in

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.687
World War Two.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.589
This is that significant.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.024
So what we're seeing here

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:58.892
is really

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.227
a transformation of the world order.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.062
The Russians,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.663
by their invasion of Ukraine,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.964
have tried to go in

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.366
and they've tried to upend

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.200
the world order.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.069
The they and the Chinese

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.336
are very much interested

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.505
in making sure that the United States

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.508
is not the dominant power in the world.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.977
And by doing this invasion of Ukraine,

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.181
you know, almost a year ago today,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:21.781
you see that

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.016
there is so many different

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.784
aspects to this.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.387
You had the initial attack on Kiev

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.788
the one that was repulsed.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:29.789
We all remember that

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.091
40 mile long

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.258
column of tanks

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.727
that was into armored personnel

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.262
carriers and trucks

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.897
that was supposed to make it to Kiev.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.632
They never made it to Kiev.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.733
And the very fact

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.469
that the president of the United States

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.303
a year

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.671
on, can say

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.573
two presidents, Alinsky on presidents.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.241
Alinsky's home turf

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.943
that we are standing by you,

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.711
that we're standing with you.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.047
That is incredibly significant

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.515
because what it shows is

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.916
that there are so many different things

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.952
so you look at, for example, the tanks

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.121
that all the allies have pledged.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.055
You know,
you've got 31

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.023
tanks from the United States, the Abrams

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.891
tanks, the Germans

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.825
with their leopard tubes,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.260
and the Canadians as well,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:07.827
and the Brits

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.395
bringing their challengers in.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.830
That's just symptomatic of

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.265
what's really going on here.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.300
Those tanks can make a big difference

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.368
on the battlefield,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.402
because what we want

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.937
the Ukrainians to do

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.373
is engage in a war of maneuver.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.642
Right now, there is a bit of a

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.209
you know,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.611
some people would call it a stalemate,

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.980
but basically the forces are stalled,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.381
especially in the east.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.583
And if they can break out of that,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.885
it would be kind of like

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.653
what happened in World War One,

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.655
where the United States came in

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.990
the tanks were invented.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.258
And that

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.792
really increased mobility

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.728
on the very static front

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.730
on the Western front in that war.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.733
And this same kind of philosophy is what

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.401
the military part of

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.736
this is going to be like.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.171
And, you know, seeing these pictures

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.672
coming out of Kiev,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.974
that not only underlines

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.876
the military dimension of this,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.511
but it also underlines

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.079
the geopolitical part of this,

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.315
which is very significant because

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.483
because the United States

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.552
is not going to go quietly

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.453
as the dominant power of the world.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.022
And we're saying to the Russians

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.924
and to anybody else who's watching

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:11.324
that we are

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.926
not only sticking with Ukraine,

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.494
but we're going to do this

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.595
for as the president

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.963
said, as long as it takes.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.499
I think the next question, Colonel, is

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.202
what else will come to get the job done

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.169
for Ukraine. Right.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.038
And the fact that Russia is tapped

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.973
almost all of its ground forces.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.474
But as our reporting show

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.309
still has

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.144
a significant air power reserve

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.612
that it hasn't tapped.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.681
Can this be won by Ukraine?

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.784
Without us F-16s?

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.953
Well, the bottom line, Poppy, on

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.821
that is probably no.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.789
And the reason I say

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.958
that is in modern warfare,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.061
the air superiority has been key

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.163
to the success of land forces.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.931
And it's also been key

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.500
to providing that a cover

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.302
for the military's

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.738
actions of whatever domain they're using.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.673
So what's remarkable

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.441
is that the Russians

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.375
haven't achieved

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:05.044
air superiority at all in anything

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:06.613
that they've done here.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.281
And when you see the, you know,

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.583
the possibility of an F-16

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.718
coming in there with,

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.653
you know, its ability to

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.121
not only hit ground targets

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.823
but hit air to air targets,

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:19.092
that becomes a significant element

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.127
of an air campaign.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.629
The problem that we have

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.263
is bringing

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.631
all these forces together

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.766
and making sure that the Ukrainians

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:27.700
have the training

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.501
that they need

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.969
in order to effectively

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.638
use this weapon system.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:32.338
And, of course,

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.606
we're seeing them do this.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.340
You know, in Britain,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.409
we have the initial

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.910
aspects of training pilots,

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.579
Ukrainian pilots.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.647
That's going to be

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.048
exceptionally important

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:43.149
to get this right.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.084
And in order for Ukraine to succeed,

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.053
I believe that air power is going to be

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.755
a significant component to that.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:49.922
And you made a very interesting

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.556
point, Poppy,

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.958
because the Russians have not used

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.027
a significant portion of their air power.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.228
Probably several reasons

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.763
of that for that.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.364
But the very fact that they're not doing

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.866
that shows that either

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.134
they have it in reserve

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.735
or it doesn't work.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.704
And if it doesn't work,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:05.705
the Russians have

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.572
major problems,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.874
even more significant

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.176
than what we've seen so far.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.244
Yesterday, U.S.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.178
Senator Lindsey Graham

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:12.879
called on the US

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.782
to start training Ukrainian pilots today

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.483
on those F-16s.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.751
Thank you very much, Colonel Leighton.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:19.819
We appreciate it very much.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.387
And for more perspective on this

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:22.922
just absolutely historic visit

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:23.423
that we are now

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.191
seeing still underway right now,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.693
I want to bring in David Sanger,

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:27.360
who is CNN's

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.161
national security

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.128
analyst and national

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.430
security correspondent

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.664
for The New York Times.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.865
David, obviously,

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.200
you and I both covered Biden

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.735
and this has been a trip

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.236
that he had been wanting to take

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.204
for about a year now.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.839
He has not done so so far.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.341
They were talking about security reasons

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:43.209
why he could not go.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:43.743
I think one

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.178
big question, though, is

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:45.912
what do you think

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.547
the reaction is like right now?

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:48.281
What's the response

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.882
happening inside the Kremlin

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:50.283
as they are

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.451
watching President Biden

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.386
on the ground with President Zelensky

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:57.690
You know, it's a fascinating question

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.325
because

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.159
President Putin

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.895
is supposed to give a speech tomorrow

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.498
that was supposed to be his rationale

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.233
for continuing a war

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.902
that has already produced about 200,000

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:12.105
Russian casualties,

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.941
including we think, 50,000 or more dead.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.609
That was not the plan.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:19.612
The plan was that, of course, Ukraine,

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.114
and he was supposed

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.383
to be Russian territory by now.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.084
And so what you're going to see

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:25.885
tomorrow are

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.755
two very different visions of

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.990
not only where the war could go,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.959
but between President Putin's speech

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.260
and then President Biden's

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.261
speech, two

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.596
very different visions

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.431
of how Europe should be organized.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.499
And that's why

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.701
this is really such a critical moment

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.835
in that

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:45.271
that the end of that post-Cold War order

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.873
we've been discussing for so long

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.110
And so President Biden

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.577
will then come

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.012
here to Poland, of course,

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.415
where he is supposed to speak tomorrow.

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.417
That's going to be a huge aspect of this

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:57.850
as well.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.818
We've talked about the role

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.553
that Poland has played, a critical role.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.221
They've had a big change

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.356
in just the last year.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.291
But a big question has been

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:07.059
where they've been funneling, of course,

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.161
these weapons

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.362
and arms

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.163
shipments that they have been

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:11.397
getting into Ukraine.

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:11.731
Obviously,

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.932
Ukraine wants to see

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.066
different levels of that.

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.601
And what the White House announced today,

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.804
the half a billion dollars in aid package

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.571
but a lot of the things

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.106
that we've seen them send before,

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.240
it obviously did not

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.108
include the longer

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:22.809
range missiles

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.243
that Ukraine is in wanting

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.546
or the F-16 fighter jets.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:27.313
They've also said that

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.315
they believe they so desperately need.

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:30.016
What are you watching

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:30.917
on that front, David?

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:33.219
Well, Caitlin, I

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.086
spent the weekend

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.788
at the Munich Security Conference,

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.990
so we had about 50 members of Congress,

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.192
a number of members

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.860
of the Cabinet, Secretary of State

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.061
Blinken, and, of course,

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:44.664
Vice President Harris, who gave a speech

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.934
calling, I think was was good evidence

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.703
that the Russians have conducted

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.505
not only war crimes,

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:55.341
but are crimes against humanity.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.076
But that leaves open the question

00:07:57.076 --> 00:07:59.011
of how far President Biden

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:02.882
is ready to go to expand their support,

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.283
because while he says

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:06.352
we're there as long as it takes,

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.421
he doesn't say what we're there with.

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:10.356
And the complaint that we heard here

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.491
from the Ukrainians

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.158
who were

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.160
at the conference in large numbers

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.596
was that they simply don't

00:08:16.596 --> 00:08:17.597
have what they need

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.966
to sustain over the long term.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:21.400
And there is, in fact,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.101
some tension

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.469
inside the White House

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.338
and inside the administration

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.672
about whether you give them

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.674
what they need for the next few months

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.109
or you give them what they need

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:30.543
to make it

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:32.578
impossible for Russia

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.881
to try something like this again.

00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:36.649
And those may be very different things.

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.518
And, of course, President Biden

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:40.920
increasingly concerned that weapons

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.421
that can reach deep inside

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:45.992
Russia could provoke a much wider war or

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:46.893
nuclear use.

